# Candidate profile for job triage
<!-- EXAMPLE. Copy to data/profile.md and replace it with your own information.
     The LLM reads this file to decide, for every job: great, normal or rejected,
     which resume to use and in which language. It can be written in any language. -->

## Goal
<!-- What you want and how urgently. It sets how generous or strict the triage is. -->
Land interviews for Data Analyst or Data Scientist roles in the next few months.
The triage can be moderate. When in doubt, the job goes in (as normal).

## About me
<!-- Education, experience, level and languages: what a recruiter would read in your resume. -->
- Ana Souza, Belo Horizonte, Brazil.
- B.Sc. in Statistics (2019–2023); thesis on demand forecasting with time series.
- Junior Data Analyst at a retail chain (2023–present): SQL, Power BI, Python.
- Level: junior (~2 years). Languages: Portuguese (native), English (intermediate, B1).

## Skills
- Languages: Python, SQL, R.
- Analysis: statistics, A/B testing, time series, regression.
- Tools: pandas, scikit-learn, Power BI, Excel, PostgreSQL, Git.

## My resumes (pick one per job)
<!-- These names (ml, data, general) are the ones shown in the email subject. They must match
     "triage.resumes" in config.json. -->
- **ml**: Data Scientist; modeling and forecasting roles.
- **data**: technical Data Analyst; SQL, pipelines, dashboards.
- **general**: business roles: BI, analytics, planning.
Language: **PT** for jobs in Brazil posted in Portuguese; **EN** for international jobs or jobs posted in English.

## Categories
<!-- GREAT = you tailor the resume (more work, so only the best ones).
     NORMAL = base resume. REJECTED = only when it clearly does not fit. -->
**GREAT**:
- Data Analyst or Data Scientist, junior or mid-level (stated in the posting), asking for SQL and Python;
- or a retail / demand forecasting role.

**NORMAL**:
- any data role with a real chance; a target role with no level stated;
- when in doubt: NORMAL.

**REJECTED**:
- senior or leadership (Lead, Head, Manager); internships;
- not a data role;
- on-site outside Minas Gerais; remote roles that require living outside Brazil.

## Preferences (they do not reject a job, they only help to decide)
- On-site or hybrid in Belo Horizonte; remote anywhere in Brazil.
- Full-time employee or contractor.